From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 21:00:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebPlayer: show the video of web pages on a display plane

Composing a scaled video into a web page and the page into Kodi's
screen takes more GPU time per frame than an RK3568 has at the video's
frame rate. Where Kodi's video goes direct to a plane, the web client's
video sinks connect to the kodi-web-video socket and hand over each
decoded DMA-BUF frame when it is due. The web player shows those frames
on the video plane, through the renderer, and the page on a plane
between the video and the GUI plane, where it covers the video except
where it is transparent. A frame goes back to its sink once no plane
shows it. When a page's video stops, the page returns to the video
plane.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
